            <div xml:id="d878">

                <pb facs="1172" n="1052" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg1052"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2184</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Denby</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my letter to you of
                    December 19,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d878-f1"/> and to your reply thereto under
                    date of December 23,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d878-f2"/> regarding the withdrawal
                    of the marine garrison at Camaguey, Cuba, I beg to advise you that the
                    Department of State is now informed by General Crowder that he is satisfied that
                    local conditions no longer require the retention of this American garrison at
                    Camaguey, and that adequate provision has been made for the protection of
                    American property in that vicinity. I beg to request, therefore, that
                    instructions may be issued in order that the withdrawal of the marine garrison
                    from Camaguey may take effect without delay.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P. Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
